:123,"bibl":124},"edition",[125,136,144],{"author":126,"date":127,"citedRange":128,"ptr":129,"ref":131,"inscriptionDate":127,"title":133,"citation":134,"uri":135,"year":127},"Bacci, Coppolino","2009","113 and 166 tav.XXXIVa",{"target":130},"https://www.zotero.org/groups/382445/items/DX8AWC9Q",{"_":132,"target":132},"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10002171","La Necropoli di Abakainon: primi dati","\u003Cspan>G.M. Bacci e P. Coppolino, \u003Ci>La Necropoli di Abakainon: primi dati\u003C/i> (Messina: Regione Siciliana, 2009)\u003C/span>","https://www.zotero.org/groups/isicily/items/DX8AWC9Q",{"author":137,"date":138,"citedRange":139,"ptr":140,"ref":142,"inscriptionDate":138,"year":34},"Sofia","2015","113 fig.115",{"target":141},"https://www.zotero.org/groups/382445/items/9QTE4E3Z",{"_":143,"target":143},"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001575",{"author":137,"date":145,"citedRange":146,"ptr":147,"ref":149,"inscriptionDate":145,"year":34},"2018","107 no.8 and fig.9",{"target":148},"https://www.zotero.org/groups/382445/items/JQQKI6JP",{"_":150,"target":150},"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001574",{"type":152,"bibl":153},"discussion",[17],{"editor":155,"principal":158,"contributors":159,"change":167},{"_":156,"ref":157},"Jonathan Prag","#JP",{"_":156,"ref":157},[160,163],{"_":156,"xml:id":161,"ref":162},"JP","http://orcid.org/0000-0003-3819-8537",{"_":164,"xml:id":165,"ref":166},"Simona Stoyanova","SS","https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3914-9569",{"_":168,"when":169,"who":170},"renumbered files, uris and references","2021-01-19","#SS",[172],{"atLeast":173,"atMost":173},59,[175,176,177],"Bacci, Coppolino, 2009, La Necropoli di Abakainon: primi dati","Sofia, 2015","Sofia, 2018",[179,180,181],"DX8AWC9Q","9QTE4E3Z","JQQKI6JP",[183,184,185,19,24,28,186,187,188,189,187,190,191,120],"isic004418","epitaph for [-?-], child of gerontios",{"_":5},"abacaenum","tripi","sicilia","sicily","necropoli di abakainon","ancient greek",[],{"title":194,"body":195,"divs":196,"editions":215,"images":225,"handnote":226},"ISic004418. Epitaph for [-?-], child of Gerontios","\u003Cdiv id=\"editions\">\u003Cdiv class=\"attribution\">Text encoding: Jonathan Prag\u003C/div>\u003Cdiv id=\"edition-interpretive\" lang=\"grc\">  \u003Cdiv class=\"textpart\" lang=\"grc\">\u003Cspan class=\"ab\" id=\"div-interpretive\">  \u003Ca id=\"al1-interpretive\">\u003C!--0-->\u003C/a>\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">1\u003C/span>[\u003Cspan dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gap\">---\u003C/span>]ς̣ \u003Cbr id=\"al2-interpretive\">\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">2\u003C/span>Γ̣ερόντιου \u003C/span>\u003C/div>  \u003Cp class=\"miniapp\">\u003C/p>\u003C/div>\u003Cdiv class=\"attribution\">Text encoding: Jonathan Prag\u003C/div>\u003Cdiv id=\"edition-diplomatic\" lang=\"grc\">\u003Cdiv class=\"textpart\" lang=\"grc\">\u003Cspan class=\"ab\" id=\"div-diplomatic\">\u003Ca id=\"al1-diplomatic\">\u003C!--0-->\u003C/a>\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">1\u003C/span>[\u003Cspan dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gap\">---\u003C/span>].\u003Cbr id=\"al2-diplomatic\">\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">2\u003C/span>.ΕΡΟΝΤΙΟΥ\u003C/span>\u003C/div>\u003Cp class=\"miniapp\">\u003C/p>\u003C/div>\u003C/div>  \u003Cdiv id=\"facsimile-images\">\u003Ch2>Facsimile Images\u003C/h2>\u003C/div>  \u003Cdiv id=\"apparatus\">\u003Ch4>Apparatus criticus\u003C/h4>\u003Cul>\u003Cli>\u003Cspan>\u003Cspan>text based upon photographs\u003C/span>\u003C/span>; \u003C/li>\u003Cli>\u003Cspan class=\"line 1\">line.1: \u003Cspan>Sofia 2018: [-----]; a horizontal is visible above the final ου of line 2, which in context is surely the remains of a final sigma (the stone shows no traces of further letters to the right).\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\u003Cbr>\u003C/li>\u003Cli>\u003Cspan class=\"line 2\">line.2: \u003Cspan>Sofia 2018: [Γ]εροντιου; the foot of a vertical stroke is clearly visible before the epsilon, and the spacing is most compatible with Γ.\u003C/span>\u003C/span>\u003C/li>\u003C/ul>\u003C/div>  \u003Cdiv id=\"translation\">\u003Ch2>English translation\u003C/h2>\u003Cp class=\"translation-author\">\u003Ca href=\"http://orcid.org/0000-0003-3819-8537\">Jonathan Prag\u003C/a>\u003C/p>  \u003Cp>[?] (child) of Gerontios\u003C/p>  \u003C/div>  \u003Cdiv id=\"commentary\">\u003Ch2>commentary\u003C/h2>  \u003Cp>Interpretation of this fragmentary text is context dependent. The text/plinth forms a pair with the adjoining plinth \u003Ca href=\"http://sicily.classics.ox.ac.uk/inscription/ISic004417\" target=\"_blank\">ISic004417\u003C/a>. On that second plinth, the genitive [---]εροντιου is legible in the second line. The only attested Greek name compatible with this is \u003Ca href=\"http://clas-lgpn2.classics.ox.ac.uk/cgi-bin/lgpn_search.cgi?name=%CE%93%CE%B5%CF%81%CF%8C%CE%BD%CF%84%CE%B9%CE%BF%CF%82\" target=\"_blank\">Γερόντιος\u003C/a>, which is known in later Roman times at Catania (\u003Ca href=\"http://sicily.classics.ox.ac.uk/inscription/ISic003199\" target=\"_blank\">ISic003199\u003C/a>) and Syracuse (\u003Ca href=\"https://www.zotero.org/groups/isicily/items/H73GNMU6\" target=\"_blank\">Orsi 1896\u003C/a>: 31 no.318) - and the restoration of a gamma at the start of line 2 of the text presented here is the obvious resolution of the traces visible on the stone. Comparison with other examples of paired monuments in this necropolis, particularly \u003Ca href=\"http://sicily.classics.ox.ac.uk/inscription/ISic004415\" target=\"_blank\">ISic004415\u003C/a>/\u003Ca href=\"http://sicily.classics.ox.ac.uk/inscription/ISic004416\" target=\"_blank\">ISic004416\u003C/a>, shows that these monuments can record siblings. It is therefore all but certain that we can restore the name Γερόντιος in line 2 of both ISic004417 and this text, and that these two plinths also record siblings. In a few cases, including ISic004415/ISic004416 and \u003Ca href=\"http://sicily.classics.ox.ac.uk/inscription/ISic001208\" target=\"_blank\">ISic001208\u003C/a>, the first name is presented in the nominative: the traces of a horizontal at the end of line 1 visible on this stone strongly suggest a final sigma, which is most likely a nominative termination (although genitive forms are also possible).\u003C/p>  \u003C/div>  \u003Cdiv id=\"bibliography\">\u003Ch2>bibliography\u003C/h2>  \u003Cul>\u003Cli> Bacci and Coppolino 2009 113 and 166 tav.XXXIVa \u003Ca href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10002171\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10002171\u003C/a>\u003C/li>\u003Cli> Sofia 2015 113 fig.115 \u003Ca href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001575\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001575\u003C/a>\u003C/li>\u003Cli> Sofia 2018 107 no.8 and fig.9 \u003Ca href=\"https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001574\" target=\"_blank\">https://biblio.inscriptiones.org/epig10001574\u003C/a>\u003C/li>\u003C/ul>  \u003Cul>\u003Cli>\u003C/li>\u003C/ul>  \u003C/div>  \u003Cdiv id=\"handnote\">\u003Cp>Neat, regular, simply cut, widely spaced letters. Epsilon has shorter middle bar; rho has closed, regular eye; omicron is small and mid-line; nu is broad with verticals of equal length.\u003C/p> Line 1-2  59  Interlineation line 1 to 2    \u003C/div>\u003Cdiv id=\"license\"> Licensed under a Creative Commons-Attribution 4.0 licence.  \u003C/div>",[197,200,203,206,209,212],{"id":198,"html":199},"editions","\u003Cdiv class=\"attribution\">Text encoding: Jonathan Prag\u003C/div>\u003Cdiv id=\"edition-interpretive\" lang=\"grc\">  \u003Cdiv class=\"textpart\" lang=\"grc\">\u003Cspan class=\"ab\" id=\"div-interpretive\">  \u003Ca id=\"al1-interpretive\">\u003C!--0-->\u003C/a>\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">1\u003C/span>[\u003Cspan dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gap\">---\u003C/span>]ς̣ \u003Cbr id=\"al2-interpretive\">\u003Cspan class=\"linenumber\">2\u003C/span>Γ̣ερόντιου \u003C/span>\u003C/div>  \u003Cp class=\"miniapp\">\u003C/p>\u003C/div>\u003Cdiv class=\"attribution\">Text encoding: Jonathan Prag\u003C/div>\u003Cdiv id=\"edition-diplomatic\" lang=\"grc\">\u003C